      "source": "SEWARD-REMINISCENCES",
      "at": "Frederick W. Seward, Reminiscences of a War-Time Statesman and Diplomat (1916), pp. 151-152: Sunday 14 April consultation after Washington knew the fort would evacuate; proclamation prepared for Monday publication. Retrospective account. https://archive.org/stream/reminiscencesofwsewa/reminiscencesofwsewa_djvu.txt"
    },
    {
      "source": "OR",
      "at": "III-1 pp. 67-68: proclamation dated 15 April and requisition that day. https://ehistory.osu.edu/books/official-records/122/0067 and /0068. [I] One day from surfacing represents deliberation/publication; if the fort holds, two days from received bombardment news substitutes for surrender news, using the 12 April opening (I-1 p. 31) to 14 April consultation interval. This counterfactual interval is inferred, not a documented holding-fort policy."
    }
